
# Environment / secrets
# Glob (.env.local*) not bare .env.local, so rollback backups such as
# .env.local.pre-<recipe>.bak — which hold the same secrets — are ignored too.
# Added 2026-06-06: the N4 migration recipe writes .env.local.pre-v2.0.0-n4.bak,
# which the bare .env.local rule left untracked-but-stageable (a git add -A hazard).
.env.local*
.env
*.env
# Roblox auth cookies — never commit; transient, tied to per-session needs
*.roblosecurity
.roblosecurity

# Per-agent path configuration (points to external world/ and meta/ directories).
# Pattern uses ** to match at any depth — agent dirs may live at PROJECT_ROOT/
# (legacy) or PROJECT_ROOT/agents/ (Phase 2.5.D layout).
**/local-paths.conf

# Temporary / scratch files
tmp_*
*.tmp
# Repo-root debug dump patterns (anchored with leading / to avoid matching
# legitimately-named files in subdirectories). Added 2026-05-07 after a
# wave of leftovers from past sessions: bitnet_*.txt, before_*.json,
# *_tmp.json, goal-selector-raw.txt, and a corrupted Windows-temp-path
# filename (fullwidth colon U+FF1A) appearing at repo root.
# 2026-05-12 extension: /tmp-* catches hyphen-prefix ad-hoc scratch files
# (tmp-rb1.json, tmp-maintain-goal.json) that LLM sessions write at repo
# root when piping JSON into reasoning-bank-add.sh / guardrails-add.sh and
# forget to delete. The unanchored tmp_* rule above (line 14) only catches
# underscore-prefix; the hyphen-prefix variant slipped through.
/before_*.json
/*_tmp.json
/*_tmp.txt
/bitnet_*.txt
/goal-selector-raw.txt
# goal-selector debug dumps (gsel_iter.json / gsel_err.txt) from manual
# `goal-selector.py >gsel_iter.json 2>gsel_err.txt` runs at repo-root CWD.
# No code creator (a debugging convenience); defensive net like
# goal-selector-raw.txt above. Added 2026-06-03 cruft cleanup.
/gsel_*
/tmp-*
# Corrupted-path artifacts: a Windows drive-letter path (e.g. C:/Users/...)
# treated as RELATIVE by POSIX/MSYS Python or bash creates a literal top-
# level entry whose ':' is filesystem-mangled. TWO manglings occur in this
# repo and BOTH must be ignored:
#   - U+F03A : Cygwin/MSYS Private-Use mapping of ':' (git-bash mkdir -p,
#     mv, redirection). This is the one actually observed on disk
#     (dir "C" + U+F03A, octal ïº). The pre-2026-05-15 rule
#     used U+FF1A and silently never matched it.
#   - U+FF1A : fullwidth colon, produced by some Python string-mangling
#     paths. Kept for defense-in-depth.
/C*
/C：*
# 2026-05-15: two more repo-root artifacts observed after an 8h multi-agent
# run, both wrong-CWD / unexpanded-path bugs (root cause is upstream; these
# nets only stop the cruft entering git, they do NOT fix the creator):
#   - /sessions/ : state-replay `cli.py download --dest ./sessions` uses a
#     RELATIVE dest (.claude/skills/state-replay/SKILL.md). Run with
#     CWD=repo-root instead of `cd .../Ayoai-State-Replay`, ~5MB of
#     game-session archives land at repo root.
#   - /SPAWN_LOG : literal 0-byte file (not "$RT_SPAWN_LOG"); in-repo code
#     only uses the $-prefixed form, so the creator is an external-repo or
#     runtime invocation with the wrong CWD/var.
/sessions/
/SPAWN_LOG

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.stackdump

# Editor files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
# Centralized bytecode cache (PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX set in _paths.sh, 2026-05-19)
# All __pycache__ contents route here instead of scattering across the tree.
core/.pycache/
# pytest cache (pinned via pytest.ini `cache_dir = core/.pytest_cache`, 2026-05-19)
core/.pytest_cache/
# Legacy unpinned pytest cache at repo root (pre-2026-05-19 pytest invocations)
.pytest_cache/
# Test tempdirs under core/scripts/tests/ (project-local tempdirs because
# OS-tempdir under C:\Users\... is unreachable from Git-Bash subprocess
# invocations — see test_iteration_commit_untracked_filter.py PROJECT_TMP)
core/scripts/tests/_tmp_*/
# Python interpreter shim (auto-created by _paths.sh on Windows; may land at repo root or in core/scripts/ depending on cwd when the shim bootstraps)
.python-shim/
core/scripts/.python-shim/

# Node artifacts
node_modules/

# File history (auto-generated by write scripts).
# ** matches both PROJECT_ROOT/<agent>/.history/ (legacy) and
# PROJECT_ROOT/agents/<agent>/.history/ (Phase 2.5.D layout).
**/.history/

# File locks (transient)
*.lock
# Directory-based locks (mkdir-atomic). The .autocompact-serialize-lock/
# dir is acquired by core/scripts/precompact-serialize.sh as a project-root
# global mutex during PreCompact; it gets stranded if a crash occurs between
# acquire and release, and prior to this rule the stranded entries were
# repeatedly committed and deleted by sibling agents (g-280-08 origin).
/.autocompact-serialize-lock/
# .iteration-commit-lock/ is acquired by core/scripts/iteration-commit.sh
# as a per-repo mutex serializing the status→add→commit critical section
# (g-280-11). Sibling-agent ping-pong risk is identical to the autocompact
# lock above — the .gitignore root rule prevents recurrence regardless of
# stale-lock crashes between acquire and trap release.
/.iteration-commit-lock/

# Ephemeral session state (recreated each session per agent).
# Pattern **/session/ matches any agent's session dir at any depth —
# PROJECT_ROOT/<agent>/session/ (legacy) or PROJECT_ROOT/agents/<agent>/session/
# (Phase 2.5.D layout).
**/session/
# Phase 2.6 per-session dirs (one per Claude Code session, dir name IS the SID).
# Contains binding.yaml + session-summary.yaml + per-session scratch.
# Recreated each session by /start; cleaned up by cleanup-stale-bindings.sh.
**/sessions/
# Agent binding files (managed by /start)
.active-agent
.active-agent-*
# Hook coordination files (one-shot breadcrumbs, consumed after reading)
.stop-hook-stdin.json
# Stop hook audit log + timing (relocated 2026-05-19 to core/logs/; legacy
# patterns kept for stragglers until Phase 1.5 cleanup). New writes go to
# core/logs/stop-hook.log and core/logs/stop-hook-timing.jsonl (already
# covered by `core/logs/` rule below).
.stop-hook-log
.stop-hook-timing.jsonl
# Hook entry-sentinel files (mtime markers for cancellation telemetry — g-115-636).
# Relocated 2026-05-19 to core/logs/hook-fires/ (already covered below).
# Legacy root path kept for stragglers.
/.hook-fires/
# Bash agent-inject hook diagnostic surface (per-SID sentinels + JSONL log).
# Relocated 2026-05-19 to core/logs/bash-inject-sentinels/ and
# core/logs/bash-inject-misses.jsonl (already covered below). Legacy patterns
# kept for stragglers.
.bash-inject-misses.jsonl
.bash-inject-no-binding-*
# SID collision diagnostic — relocated 2026-05-19 to
# core/logs/sid-collisions.jsonl. Legacy root path kept for stragglers.
.sid-collisions.jsonl
# LLM ad-hoc scratch dirs (NEVER intended at repo root — created by
# autonomous agents writing JSON dumps during goal execution). Phase 0.21
# closes the staging-allowlist gap; Phase 1 will git-rm and delete.
/.migration-tmp/
/.runtime-tmp/
# Crash recovery markers (written by StopFailure hook, consumed by /boot).
# Pattern uses ** for both legacy and Phase 2.5.D layouts.
**/session/crash-marker

# Forged skills (domain-specific, registered in world/forged-skills.yaml)
.claude/skills/operator-health-trend/

# Runtime logs — per-agent watchdog logs, stderr captures, dated investigation
# artifacts. Regenerated per session; should never ship in a packaged framework.
# Un-tracked 2026-05-17 (Phase 1.6 packaging cleanup) after audit found 15
# files including dated investigation artifacts had been committed.
core/logs/

# Claude Code agent-worktree markers — ephemeral runtime entries per spawned
# subagent. Un-tracked 2026-05-17; never shipped in packaging.
.claude/worktrees/

# Safety net: world/ and meta/ should never exist at repo root
# (they live at external paths configured in local-paths.conf)
/world/
/meta/

# .mind-data/ — local storage root (asp-330 ".mind-data/ Universal Storage
# Architecture", M3 init convention). When PROJECT_ROOT/.mind-data/ exists it is
# the storage root by convention (world -> .mind-data/world, meta -> .mind-data/meta;
# resolved by _paths.py/_paths.sh/agent_paths.py `_resolve_tier`, M1 g-330-01).
# It mirrors the external world/meta storage — local, machine-specific, never
# committed (publishing it would ship one machine's full knowledge tree + meta
# strategies). The whole subtree is ignored, including the optional
# .mind-data/.env.local override and any .mind-data/agents/ migrated via the M4
# `--agent-dirs` migration (migrate-to-mind-data.sh).
/.mind-data/

# framework-runtime — transient PID/port/log files (one per repo)
# Relocated 2026-05-19 (Phase 2 daemon consolidation): .runtime/ → mind_api/state/
/mind_api/state/

# Benchmark results (per-run JSON dumps)
# Relocated 2026-05-19 (Phase 2 daemon consolidation): bench/ → mind_api/bench/
/mind_api/bench/results/

# Seed transplant backup directories — created by core/scripts/seed-transplant.sh
# at destination before overwrite. Timestamped, one per transplant invocation.
# Must never be committed: each backup contains the FULL UNTRANSFORMED source
# tree (publishing them would defeat the seed transformation entirely).
# Discovered in Phase 6 fresh-eyes review 2026-05-20.
.seed-backup-*/

# Transient transplant staging/unpack dirs — created by core/scripts/_transplant_pack.py
# during offline pack (stage under PROJECT_ROOT) and land (unpack under dest.parent).
# Normally removed in the engine's finally block; ignored for crash safety, same as
# the seed-backup pattern above.
.transplant-stage-*/
.transplant-unpack-*/

# Machine-local Claude Code settings (per-machine permissions + hardcoded
# user-path allowlists). Per CLAUDE.md, this is the constitutional anchor —
# agent MUST NOT edit, and the file's per-machine paths (C:/.../Ayoai-Mind etc.)
# would actively break any other user's deployment if shipped.
# Discovered in Phase 6 fresh-eyes review 2026-05-20.
.claude/settings.local.json
